        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "measure-for-measure/sceneIV_21.6/p@139555",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "FRIAR PETER.\nCome, I have found you out a stand most fit,\nWhere you may have such vantage on the Duke\nHe shall not pass you. Twice have the trumpets sounded.\nThe generous and gravest citizens\nHave hent the gates, and very near upon\nThe Duke is entering. Therefore hence, away.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
